# apply-agent build contracts

Python 3.14 package `agent/` in this repo, run with `.venv/bin/python` (never system python, never a new venv).
Sync Playwright API only (no asyncio). Config is `config.yaml`, facts about the applicant are `profile.yaml`,
secrets are `.env` (never print secret values; read them via `os.environ` after `agent.config` loads dotenv).

## Already built (do not rewrite; extend only with additive changes and say so in your report)
- `agent/config.py`: `ROOT, DATA_DIR, SCREENSHOT_DIR, DB_PATH, LOG_DIR, load_config(), load_profile(), gemini_settings(), parse_duration()`
- `agent/models.py`: `Job, Field, Answer, ApplyResult, ApplyStatus, detect_ats(), normalize_url(), dedupe_key()`.
  `Field.key` is the value of the `data-aa-key` attribute stamped on the DOM element.
  `Answer.source` is one of `profile | bank | generated | unknown`.
- `agent/db.py`: SQLite helpers (`upsert_jobs, next_jobs, set_job_status, record_application, kv_get/kv_set,
  get_account_row/put_account_row/set_account_verified, mail_is_seen/mark_mail_seen, add_captcha_spend/captcha_spend_since, night_start`).
- `agent/llm.py`: `generate_text(prompt)`, `generate_json(prompt, schema, images=None, model=None)`, `vision_model()`,
  `available()`, `LLMUnavailable`. Has timeouts + circuit breaker. Always catch `LLMUnavailable` and degrade.
- `agent/browser.py`: `open_browser(config, visible=False)` context manager -> BrowserContext; `new_page(ctx)`; `human_pause()`.
- `agent/ats/base.py`: `ApplyContext(page, browser, config, profile, submit_mode, dry_run, run_id)`,
  `submit_decision(fields, answers, mode, dry_run) -> (bool, reason)`, `blocked_result(...)`, `Adapter` protocol.

## Interfaces each owner must implement exactly (other modules import these names)

`agent/sources/*.py` each expose `fetch(config: dict) -> list[Job]`. Job ids are stable: `f"{source}:{native_id}"`
or `f"{source}:" + sha1(normalize_url(url))[:16]`.
`agent/filters.py`: `keep(job, config) -> tuple[bool, str]`, `filter_jobs(jobs, config) -> list[Job]`.
`agent/fetch.py`: `fetch_all(config) -> dict` with keys `fetched, matched, new, by_source` (calls `db.upsert_jobs`).

`agent/form.py`:
- `extract_fields(scope, root: str | None = None) -> list[Field]` (scope = Page or Frame; stamps `data-aa-key`)
- `fill_fields(scope, fields: list[Field], answers: list[Answer]) -> list[str]` (returns keys that failed to fill)
- `page_text(page, max_chars: int = 8000) -> str` (visible job-description text)
- `click_text(scope, texts: list[str], roles=("button","link")) -> bool`
`agent/answers.py`:
- `answer_fields(fields, job, profile, *, job_text: str = "", extra_context: str = "") -> list[Answer]`
  (deterministic profile/answer_bank matching first, Gemini for the rest; factual unknowns -> source "unknown",
  never invent facts; essays/opinions may be "generated"; resume file inputs -> `profile["resume_path"]`)
- `resume_text() -> str` (cached pypdf extraction of the resume)
`agent/captcha.py`:
- `@dataclass CaptchaOutcome(status: "none"|"solved"|"failed"|"budget"|"unsupported", kind: str = "", cost: float = 0.0, detail: str = "")`
- `solve_if_present(page, config, job_id: str | None = None) -> CaptchaOutcome`
`agent/mail.py`:
- `@dataclass Verification(code: str | None, link: str | None, message_id: str, subject: str, sender: str)`
- `wait_for_verification(after_ts: float, *, sender_hint: str | None = None, to_alias: str | None = None, timeout: float | None = None, want: "code"|"link"|"any" = "any") -> Verification | None`
- `authorize_interactive() -> None`, `available() -> bool`
`agent/vault.py`:
- `@dataclass Account(tenant_key, email, password, company, login_url, verified: bool)`
- `tenant_key_for(url) -> str`, `get(tenant_key) -> Account | None`,
  `create(tenant_key, company, login_url, *, plus_alias: bool = True) -> Account`,
  `mark_verified(tenant_key)`, `update_email(tenant_key, email)`, `alias_email(company) -> str`
Adapters `agent/ats/<name>.py` expose a module-level `ADAPTER` object implementing `Adapter`
(`name`, `can_handle(job)`, `apply(job, ctx) -> ApplyResult`). Adapters call `captcha.solve_if_present` before
the final submit, use `submit_decision` to decide, and never raise for ordinary page problems.

## File ownership (only edit files you own; create tests under `tests/test_<area>.py`)
- sources builder: `agent/sources/*`, `agent/filters.py`, `agent/fetch.py`
- forms builder: `agent/form.py`, `agent/answers.py`, `agent/captcha.py`, `agent/ats/greenhouse.py`, `agent/ats/lever.py`, `agent/ats/ashby.py`
- accounts builder: `agent/mail.py`, `agent/vault.py`, `agent/ats/workday.py`
- generic builder: `agent/ats/generic.py`
- main agent (not a subagent): `agent/__main__.py`, `agent/runner.py`, `agent/scheduler.py`, `agent/notify.py`,
  `agent/report.py`, `agent/ats/registry.py`, systemd files, `config.yaml`
If you need a change in a file you don't own, describe it in your final report instead of editing it.

## Safety rules while building and testing
- NEVER click a final "Submit application" button on a real posting. Test with `dry_run=True` or `submit_mode="fill_only"`.
- At most 2 real accounts may be created on real sites during testing; they must be saved through `vault.py`.
- Network note (eduroam): `agent.config` reroutes `*.googleapis.com` DNS to reachable Google front ends.
  On this network HTTP/1.1 to those hosts hangs and Python HTTP/2 (httpx+h2) stalls on request bodies over a
  few KB, while `curl --http2` is reliable. Gemini goes through `agent.llm` (curl transport, never call it
  directly). For Gmail and OAuth: GET requests and small POSTs via `httpx.Client(http2=True)` work; do not
  use httplib2 / `googleapiclient.discovery` transports. IMAP to imap.gmail.com is blocked. Unit tests must mock `agent.llm` and Gmail; code must degrade gracefully
  (LLM down -> unknown answers -> job queued, not crashed).
- Keep comments sparse; match the style of `agent/db.py` and `agent/ats/base.py`.
